# Backend-only repository. Review is required from someone who owns the
# area being changed -- GitHub enforces this automatically once branch
# protection on main requires a review from code owners.
#
# Fill in real usernames/teams below before this has any effect; a
# CODEOWNERS file with no owners is silently inert.
#
# NOTE: every path below was previously prefixed with a backend/ directory,
# left over from before the frontend/mobile split. There is no backend/
# directory any more -- this repository
# root IS the backend -- so those rules matched nothing and the payments,
# security and migration paths they claim to protect were unowned.
# Branch protection's "require review from code owners" would have passed
# them straight through. Paths are now repo-root-relative and verified to
# exist.

# Default: unassigned. Replace with a general backend maintainer.
* @REPLACE-ME-default-owner

# CI/CD and deployment surface -- changes here affect how everything ships.
/.github/                @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner
/k8s/                     @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner
/argocd/                  @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner
/Dockerfile        @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner
/Dockerfile.celery  @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner
/docker-compose.yml        @REPLACE-ME-platform-owner

# Payments / wallet -- the highest-consequence code in this repository.
/api/views/wallet.py       @REPLACE-ME-payments-owner
/api/views/direct_debit.py  @REPLACE-ME-payments-owner
/api/models/wallet.py       @REPLACE-ME-payments-owner
/api/models/contest.py      @REPLACE-ME-payments-owner
/api/integrations/telebirr/ @REPLACE-ME-payments-owner

# Secrets / crypto -- security-sensitive, warrants a security-focused review.
/infrastructure/    @REPLACE-ME-security-owner
/common/security/    @REPLACE-ME-security-owner

# Database migrations -- irreversible once applied to production.
/api/migrations/    @REPLACE-ME-backend-owner
